# Project
target/

# Repository-local git worktrees. Tooling puts a second checkout under `.worktrees/<name>`, which
# left untracked makes `git status --short` report it — the condition RELEASING.md requires to be
# clean before tagging. `run_ci_local.sh` already bounds its workflow scan away from this path.
.worktrees/

# Local planning notes (not for distribution)
notes/

# Session indexes and real transcripts. An index holds whole conversations, which are
# private and large, and a transcript copied out of ~/.claude, ~/.codex, or ~/.cursor is
# someone's real session content. Test fixtures are written synthetically instead — see
# tests/aise-demo/projects/, whose ids and paths are obviously fake (cafe0001-cafe-...,
# -Users-demo-webauth), and the Rust tests, which build corpora in tempfile::tempdir().
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.update.lock
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.jsonl
!tests/aise-demo/projects/**/*.jsonl

# Demo recording outputs (regenerate with: uv run python tests/test_demo.py --record)
demo.cast
demo.gif
demo.mp4
*.cast
*.gif
*.mp4
*.webm

